      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\n  Draft Phase 2 implementation for #49529: adopt `ldmatrix.s8.s4` in\r\n  Machete’s W4A8-INT8 path.\r\n\r\n  The initial commit enables only the narrow Machete QQQ\r\n  configuration needed to instantiate and test the Phase 2 path:\r\n\r\n  - INT8 activations and `uint4b8` weights.\r\n  - FP16 group scales with group size 128.\r\n  - FP32 channel and token scales.\r\n  - One fixed `128x16`, `1x1x1` H100-oriented schedule.\r\n  - Focused correctness coverage for `M=64`, `K=4096`, `N=4096`.\r\n\r\n  Subsequent commits in this draft will add the W4A8 prepacked-layout\r\n  update, the `ldmatrix.s8.s4` shared-memory-to-register copy atom, bit-\r\n  exact coverage, and H100 validation.\r\n\r\n  This does not duplicate #50096: that PR changes Marlin, while this work\r\n  implements the separate Machete Phase 2 path.\r\n\r\n  Related to #49529.\r\n\r\n  ## Test Plan\r\n\r\n  - Build vLLM with the generated Machete QQQ specialization.\r\n  - Run:\r\n\r\n    ```bash\r\n    .venv/bin/python -m pytest \\\r\n      tests/kernels/quantization/test_machete_mm.py \\\r\n      -v -k test_machete_qqq\r\n\r\n  - Add bit-exact packed-nibble coverage after the copy atom is implemented.\r\n  - Validate on H100.\r\n  - Collect and report performance data only after CUDA 13.4 GA.\r\n\r\n  ## Test Result\r\n\r\n  Passed:\r\n\r\n  - pre-commit run --files csrc/libtorch_stable/quantization/machete/\r\n    generate.py tests/kernels/quantization/test_machete_mm.py\r\n\r\n  - pre-commit run mypy-3.12 --files csrc/libtorch_stable/quantization/\r\n    machete/generate.py tests/kernels/quantization/test_machete_mm.py\r\n    --hook-stage manual\r\n\r\n  - git diff --check\r\n\r\n  Pending:\r\n\r\n  - CUDA build and targeted H100 correctness test.\r\n  - Bit-exact copy-atom coverage.\r\n  - Model-level evaluation, if the completed path becomes selected by a\r\n    supported quantization flow.\r\n\r\n  - Performance comparison after CUDA 13.4 GA.\r\n\r\n  ## Documentation\r\n\r\n  No user-facing documentation update is needed for this internal kernel\r\n  implementation.\r\n",
